# Found by a hunt: a def's end is known by line only, so a call written
# after a def's `end` on that line was put in that def and freed by it:
# register runs as the class loads, not in boot; footer is in the live
# run, not helper; launch follows start's multi-line `end`. A call on the
# line a def ends names no caller (DEC-751).
dead app Report#footer=single-caller^ Report#register=single-caller^ Report#launch=single-caller^ Report#helper=unreferenced^ Report#boot=unreferenced^ Report#start=unreferenced^
